DarkMatter <DarkMatter@thebarattheendoftheuniverse.org> writes:

>   Is there a switch to be changed for compiling with the explore
> ("wizard mode") features enabled for exploration experimentation, or
> is there a certain command key sequence for the current binaries?

Notice that explore mode is NOT the same as wizard mode.
In explore mode you don't have any of the additional wizard mode commands,
only the choice to refuse to die. And the initial wand of wishing, if you
start the game with the -X option (as opposed to switching to explore mode
with the X command when the game was not started that way).

Like Philipp said, the section 2 in include/config.h defines whether or
not wizard mode is compiled in and what is the player name needed,
but I *suppose* all official binaries are compiled with wizard mode
enabled and wizard as the relevant player name.

